# Revisions to skip in `git blame` — bulk mechanical edits that touch many lines
# without changing their meaning, so blame reports the last SUBSTANTIVE author.
#
# ENABLE IT (per-clone, and the file alone does nothing without this):
#     git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS. The 2026-08-12 VL re-id added a leading `| VL<n> |` id cell to all
# 108 VALIDATION_LEDGER.md data rows. It was line-count preserving and content-keyed, but
# it made one commit the last toucher of every ledger row, so `git blame` attributed the
# whole file to it. Session D established the damage is MASKING rather than loss:
# `git blame --ignore-rev 1ec042e` restores the underlying owners.
#
# LIMIT, stated because it is the part that bites: `blame.ignoreRevsFile` is per-clone
# config, so this file is INERT for anyone who has not run the command above. And
# unmasking does not always yield a lane — rows written before the per-lane git identities
# resolve to the shared "Joseph Bailey" author regardless (BEN-160). Two independent
# causes; this file addresses only the first.

